```
Title: AppLocker Application Would Have Been Blocked
Author: heyyanu
Date: 2026-03-26
Level: low
Description: Detects when AppLocker "Audit only" enforcement mode reports that an Application, DLL, Script, MSI,
 or Packaged-App would have been blocked if AppLocker "Enforce rules" enforcement mode was enabled.
 This rule triggers on the AppLocker audit events and requires review of the reported path against the local AppLocker policy.
 Since this rule triggers solely on event IDs without path-based filtering, tuning and false positive
 suppression must be handled at the AppLocker policy level by the policy author, not via Sigma filters.
 Analysts should review the reported FullFilePath and correlate with the local AppLocker policy to
 determine whether the activity is expected or warrants investigation.
MITRE Tactic: Execution
Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1204.002, attack.t1059.001, attack.t1059.003, attack.t1059.005, attack.t1059.006, attack.t1059.007
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/builtin/applocker/win_applocker_application_would_have_been_blocked.yml
 False Positives:
   - Expected during AppLocker policy testing and audit mode deployments
   - Legitimate system DLLs and applications not yet covered by the AppLocker policy (e.g. Windows system components, third-party software). False positives must be handled at the AppLocker policy level by the policy author, not via Sigma filters.
```
EventID IN (8003, 8006, 8021, 8024)